Build the tests, fuzz targets and benchmarks only where they can run.

The tests, the fuzz targets and the benchmarks are built with the
library and run on the machine that builds them.  A cross build cannot
run them, and building them for zedBSD stopped at the benchmark helper,
which uses CLOCK_PROCESS_CPUTIME_ID, a clock zedBSD's C library does not
have.  That part of meson.build is now used only when Meson can run the
host's programs; a native build is unchanged.

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -874,6 +874,9 @@
                output: 'xkeyboard-config-test',
                configuration: xkct_config)
 
+# Tests, fuzz targets and benchmarks, which run on the machine that builds
+# them; a cross build, which cannot run them, leaves them out.
+if meson.can_run_host_binaries()
 # Tests
 test_env = environment()
 test_env.set('XKB_LOG_LEVEL', 'debug')
@@ -1397,6 +1400,10 @@
   )
 endif
 
+else
+# The summary below reports this; no tests means none of these either.
+has_merge_modes_tests = false
+endif # meson.can_run_host_binaries()
 
 # Documentation.
 if get_option('enable-docs')
